m/u/10887688?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri","html_url":"https://github.com/josefri","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/josefri/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T17:15:31Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T17:15:31Z","body":"I don't think it needs to be unified, if it's possible to read out the settings. \n\n\nI think it's quite frustrating for users coming from other engines/3D software to use another setting for 3D navigation. \n\n\nIn the end, it's just a simple editor camera, it should not be to hard to make a dynamic mapping for it. \n\n\nIt would also be fine, if we would have two equal settings to adjust it twice.  \n\nI only discovered it, because I wanted to see if I can ditch my own implementation ^^\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722057718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2722120333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104063#issuecomment-2722120333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104063","id":2722120333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iQEKN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips",